The Stop Ladder informs Method 2–5 and 8: full responsibility and existing guarantees, direct solutions judged by behavior/failure handling/state lifetime, concrete gaps, effective defenses, and sufficient verification and completion. The uncertainty guidance informs inspection of unclear protections, avoiding invented consumers for optional manifests, and safe in-scope correction in Method 3 and 7. The eight-step structure, domain-specific checks, and bounded retry wording are local adaptations. Harness authority, authorization, current-call/JIT checks, read-only review, single-outcome Handler roles, and Router/Resolver lifecycle boundaries take precedence. No upstream modes, Guard hooks, locks, delegation controls, or STSS editing protocol are adopted.

